cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Analysis code for "Optical Quality Metrics for Detecting Instrument
  Segmentation Failure in Endoscopic Spine Surgery"
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/samersalman/sea-optical-reliability-gate
version: 1.0.0
# No doi: field yet. The Zenodo DOI is minted when the GitHub release v1.0.0 is
# archived; add it here (and to the manuscript Code Availability Statement) after
# that release exists. date-released is also left out until the release date is known.
abstract: >-
  Analysis pipeline for a retrospective external-validation study of whether
  interpretable optical image-quality measurements can flag unreliable
  instrument segmentations in endoscopic spine surgery, using the public
  Spine Endoscopic Atlas (SEA). The repository holds the R and Python code,
  the locked analysis settings, derived per-frame tables and aggregate
  results. Apart from the six example frames drawn in Figure 1B, the SEA
  images and masks are not included, and the trained checkpoints are
  distributed as GitHub release assets rather than in the repository tree.
keywords:
  - endoscopic spine surgery
  - surgical instrument segmentation
  - artificial intelligence
  - optical image quality
  - segmentation failure detection
  - external validation
  - uncertainty quantification
